<title>UK: Ecuador eyes $500 mln 10-year bond -bankers.</title>
<headline>Ecuador eyes $500 mln 10-year bond -bankers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador has taken bids for a $500 million 10-year international bond issue, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>A mandate for the deal could be awarded this week, they said. Ecuador could tap the markets fairly quickly to take advantage of positive sentiment towards emerging market credits, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;Ecuador should decide by mid-week who will lead manage their dollar deal,&quot; an emerging market debt trader said. &quot;They may come to the market quite soon because things are looking very good.&quot;</p>
<p>Ecuador first came to the market in April, when it raised $500 million via two bonds lead managed by Chase.</p>
<p>A $350 million five-year bond was priced to yield 470 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes. A $150 million seven-year FRN paid 475 b.p. over six-month Libor.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
